SECTION 3 Value-Added Telecommunications Business

text_en:
Article 22 (Reporting of value-added telecommunications business)
A person who intends to operate the value-added telecommunications business shall report thereon (including cases of reporting through information and telecommunications networks) to the Minister of Science and ICT, in accordance with conditions and procedures prescribed by Presidential Decree. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Oct. 15, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017>
Notwithstanding paragraph (1), a person who intends to manage the business of providing a special type of value-added telecommunications services shall file for registration (including registration through information and communications networks) with the Minister of Science and ICT along with the following: <Added on May 19, 2011; Mar. 23, 2013; Oct. 15, 2014; Dec. 1, 2015; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 9, 2020; Jun. 10, 2022; Mar. 18, 2025>
An implementation plan to take technical measures to comply with Article 22-3 (1) hereof and Article 104 of the Copyright Act (limited to persons providing services that fall under subparagraph 14 (a) of Article 2) ;
1-2.
An implementation plan to take technical measures to prevent the false caller's phone number by forgery, etc. (limited to persons providing services that fall under subparagraph 14 (b) of Article 2) ;
Human resources and physical facilities necessary for performing duties;
Financial soundness;
Transmission qualification certificate under Article 22-11 (3) (limited to business operators under Article 22-11 (1));
Other matters prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as a business plan.
Where the Minister of Science and ICT accepts registration of the value-added telecommunications business under paragraph (2), he or she may attach necessary conditions for the compliance with the matters prescribed in each subparagraph of that paragraph. <Added on May 19, 2011; Mar. 23, 2013; Oct. 15, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017; Mar. 18, 2025>
The Minister of Science and ICT or the Korea Media and Communications Commission shall, according to their respective jurisdictions, have public officials under their control regularly inspect at least once a year the compliance with the registration requirements under each subparagraph of paragraph (2) and the implementation status of the conditions under paragraph (3), as prescribed by Presidential Decree, and may order a person operating a business providing special value-added telecommunications services to submit relevant materials if necessary for the inspection. In such cases, Article 51 shall apply mutatis mutandis to the procedures and methods for conducting the inspection. <Added on Mar. 18, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
Notwithstanding paragraph (1), any of the following persons shall be deemed to have filed a report on the value-added telecommunications business: <Amended on Oct. 15, 2014; Mar. 18, 2025>
A person who intends to operate the small-scale value-added telecommunications business, the capital of which falls under the criteria prescribed by Presidential Decree;
A facilities-based telecommunications business operator who intends to operate the value-added telecommunications business.
A person who has filed a report on the value-added telecommunications business pursuant to paragraph (1) and a person who has filed for registration of the value-added telecommunications business pursuant to paragraph (2) shall commence business within one year after he or she filed a report on, or filed for registration of, such business. <Amended on May 19, 2011; Oct. 15, 2014; Mar. 18, 2025>
Upon receipt of a report on a value-added telecommunications business under paragraph (1) from a person who intends to manage the business of providing online video services, the Minister of Science and ICT shall notify the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism and the Korea Media and Communications Commission thereof within three months from receipt of such report. The foregoing shall also apply where a report on modification under Article 23 or a report on transfer or acquisition, etc. of business under Article 24 is received. <Added on Jun. 10, 2022; Mar. 18, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
A report filed under paragraph (1), requirements and procedures for filing for registration under paragraph (2), and other necessary matters shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree. <Added on May 19, 2011; Oct. 15, 2014; Jun. 10, 2022; Mar. 18, 2025>

