text_en:
A value-added telecommunications business operator without a domicile or place of business in the Republic of Korea that meets the standards prescribed in Article 22-7 (1) shall designate in writing a person that acts on its behalf with respect to the following matters (hereinafter referred to as "domestic agent"): <Amended on Jan. 3, 2023>
Securing a means of communication in the Republic of Korea to deal with the user’s request under Article 22-7 (1);
Submission of data under Article 22-7 (3) and (4);
Affairs related to the protection of users under Article 32 (1);
Implementation of an order to submit data under the latter part of Article 32 (2).
A domestic agent shall have a domicile or place of business in the Republic of Korea; in such cases, where any of the following corporations exists, a value-added telecommunications business operator that is required to designate a domestic agent pursuant to paragraph (1) shall designate a person selected from among such corporations as a domestic agent: <Amended on Jun. 10, 2022>
A domestic corporation established by a value-added telecommunications business operator that is required to designate a domestic agent pursuant to paragraph (1);
A domestic corporation, over which a value-added telecommunications business operator that is required to designate a domestic agent pursuant to paragraph (1), exercises dominant influence in terms of the composition of executive officers, the operation of the business, and other relevant matters.
Where a domestic agent violates this Act in relation to the subparagraphs of paragraph (1), such violation shall be deemed to have been committed by the value-added telecommunications business operator who designated the relevant domestic agent.
A domestic agent shall secure a valid means of communication with a value-added telecommunications business operator under paragraph (1). <Added on Jan. 3, 2023>
[This Article Added on Jun. 9, 2020]

