To promote safe living environment and to protect urban landscape, a telecommunications business operator and a facility management authority shall maintain cables installed on utility poles (hereafter referred to as "aerial cables" in this Article). <Amended on Dec. 11, 2018>
To ensure the systematic maintenance prescribed in paragraph (1), the Minister of Science and ICT shall formulate a maintenance plan for aerial cables (hereafter referred to as "maintenance plan" in this Article), including the following matters, each year. In such cases, the plan shall undergo deliberation by the Council for Maintenance of Aerial Cables comprised of the relevant authorities and related telecommunications business operators: <Amended on Jul. 26, 2017; Dec. 11, 2018>
Basic direction-setting for, and objectives of, the maintenance plan;
Standards for installing, removing, and recycling aerial cables;
Inspection and assessment of the maintenance status of aerial cables;
Other matters necessary for maintenance of aerial cables.
A telecommunications business operator and a facility management authority shall comply with the maintenance plan, and the burden of expenses incurred in implementing the maintenance plan shall be shared among persons who provide and use the relevant equipment, etc., as prescribed by Presidential Decree.
Matters necessary for the organization, operation, etc. of the Council for Maintenance of Aerial Cables prescribed in paragraph (2) shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree.
[This Article Added on Jan. 20, 2015]

