In any of the following cases, mediation shall be terminated:
Where an agreement is reached through recommendation for agreement under Article 45-5 (5);
Where the Dispute Mediation Committee deems that it is impracticable for the parties to reach an agreement on the relevant mediation case;
2-2.
Where an ex officio decision of mediation is made under Article 45-6 ;
Where the Dispute Mediation Committee rejects mediation under Article 45-7 ;
Where any party fails to express his or her intention to accept a proposal for mediation within the specified period under Article 45-8 (2) or expresses his or her intention to refuse to accept it;
Where an agreement is reached through mediation under Article 45-8 (3);
Where a judgment is made final and conclusive regarding a lawsuit over a dispute subject to mediation.
Where mediation is terminated pursuant to paragraph (1), the Dispute Mediation Committee shall notify the parties of such fact, specifically stating the termination and the grounds therefor.
