text_en:
Where the Korea Media and Communications Commission is notified or becomes aware that a failure to implement a recommendation under Article 32-13 (8) or a violation of Article 32-12 (1), 32-13 (2), (3) or (5), and 32-14 (1), (3) or (5), 32-15 (2) or (3), or 50 (1), it may order the public officials under its control to conduct a fact-finding investigation necessary for the verification thereon. <Amended on Jan. 21, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
The Korea Media and Communications Commission may require public officials under its control to enter the offices or places of business of any of the following persons to inspect books, documents, and other materials or articles for the investigation under paragraph (1): <Amended on Jan. 21, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
A telecommunications business operator (including an affiliate of a mobile communications business operator);
An agent and sales store of a mobile communications business operator (including their affiliate);
A mobile communications terminal device manufacturer;
A person that handles the tasks of a telecommunications business operator on entrustment, other than an agent or sales store under paragraph (2) (limited to a person that handles the tasks entrusted by a telecommunications business operator if the tasks entrusted by the telecommunications business operator are related to Article 50 ; hereafter in this Article the same shall apply).
Where the Korea Media and Communications Commission intends to conduct a fact-finding investigation under paragraph (1), it shall notify the person subject to investigation of an investigation plan, including a period of, reasons for, and details of the investigation no later than seven days before such investigation; provided, this shall not apply in cases of emergency or in cases where it is deemed that any prior notification could make it impossible to attain the purposes of such investigation through destruction of evidence, etc. <Amended on Jan. 21, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
