text_en:
Article 51-3 (Corrective order to mobile communications business operators)
Where a mobile communications business operator, an agent, or a sales store is deemed to have committed a violation against Article 32-11 (1) or 32-15 (1), the Minister of Science and ICT may issue an order to correct it.
Where it is deemed that there is a violation against Article 32-12 (1), 32-13 (2), (3), and (5), 32-14 (1), (3), and (5), or Article 32-15 (2) or (3), the Korea Media and Communications Commission may order a mobile communications business operator (including its affiliate), agent, sales store, or mobile communications terminal device manufacturer to take any of the following measures; provided, where issuing an order to take any of the following measures under the subparagraphs 1 through 3 and 6, it shall hear the opinion of the Minister of Science and ICT: <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
Disclosure of information on the sale of mobile communications services and mobile communications terminal devices;
Conclusion, implementation, or modification of the content of, an agreement between a mobile communications business operator (including their affiliate) and an agent, a sales store, or a mobile communications terminal device manufacturer;
Modification to a mobile communications business operator' terms and conditions of use or to their articles of incorporation;
Suspension of a violation;
Publication that a corrective measure has been ordered as a result of a violation;
Improving business procedures of a mobile communications business operator (including their affiliate), agent, sales store, or mobile communications terminal device manufacturer;
Prohibition of new recruitment of users (the period of prohibition shall not exceed three months, and the prohibition shall be limited to where the same offense occurs repeatedly on at least three occasions despite the measures prescribed in subparagraphs 1 through 6 or where it is obviously impracticable to prevent the loss to users only by taking such measures);
Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree as necessary to take measures prescribed in subparagraphs 1 through 7.
A mobile communications business operator (including its affiliates), an agent, a sales store, or mobile communications terminal device manufacturer shall comply with an order of the Korea Media and Communications Commission issued under paragraph (2) within the period prescribed by Presidential Decree; provided,, where the Korea Media and Communications Commission deems it impossible for the relevant business operator to comply with the order within such period due to a natural disaster or any other extenuating circumstance, the period may be extended only once. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
Before issuing an order to take any of the measures under paragraph (2), the Korea Media and Communications Commission shall notify the party of the content of the measure and give them an opportunity to state their opinions within a fixed period, and, if deemed necessary, may request the attendance of interested persons or witnesses to hear their opinions and request an appraiser to conduct appraisal; provided, the same shall not apply if the party fails to comply with such request without good cause. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
If five years elapse from the date of end of an act in violation of Article 32-12 (1), 32-13 (2), (3) or (5), 32-14 (1), (3) or (5), or Article 32-15 (2) or (3), the Korea Media and Communications Commission shall not impose any measure under paragraph (2) or a penalty surcharge under Article 52-3 for the relevant act; provided, if a measure has already been completed or the imposition of a penalty surcharge is revoked or withdrawn by a ruling on administrative appeal or a court ruling, a new disposition may be imposed in line with the purport of such ruling until two years elapse from the date the ruling becomes final and conclusive. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
[This Article Added on Jan. 21, 2015]

