text_en:
Article 83-2 (Notice of fact that communication user information is provided)
The prosecutor, the head of the investigative agency, or the head of the intelligence and investigation agency who is provided with communication user information under Article 83 (3) (hereinafter referred to as "investigation agency, etc.") shall notify the person, who is the subject of the communication user information, of the following matters in writing or by electronic means, such as text messages and messengers, within 30 days from the date on which the communication user information is provided (where the notice is deferred under paragraph (2), referring to the date on which the deferred period of notice is expired under paragraph (3)):
The main content of inquiry of communication user information and the purpose of use;
The person provided with communication user information;
The date on which the communication user information is provided.
Notwithstanding paragraph (1), an investigation agency, etc. may defer giving notice in any of the following cases:
Where national security and public safety are likely to be endangered;
Where the lives or physical safety of the victims or other related parties in the case are likely to be jeopardized;
Where the implementation of a fair judicial process is likely to be hindered by the destruction of evidence, escape, threatening of witnesses, etc.;
Where the name or privacy of the criminal suspect, victim, or other related parties in the case are likely to be infringed upon;
Where it is likely to interfere with or unduly delay the progress of administrative procedures, such as inquiries and investigations.
The deferred period of notice under paragraph (2) shall be as follows:
Where any ground referred to in paragraph (2) 1 or 2 exists: The period until the relevant ground ceases to exist;
Where any ground referred to in paragraph (2) 3 through 5 exists: A period determined each time by up to three months only two occasions.
Where the head of an intelligence and investigation agency is provided with communication user information for the purpose of collecting information aimed at preventing any harm to national security and where any of the following is applicable to the person who is the subject of the communication user information, the head of the intelligence and investigation agency need not give notice, notwithstanding paragraph (1):
A country hostile to the Republic of Korea, a foreign organization or entity and a foreign national suspected of anti-State activities, or a Korean national associated therewith;
A member of a group in the Korean Peninsula to which the de facto sovereignty of the Republic of Korea does not extend or a member of its affiliated organization located in a foreign country or a Korean national associated therewith.
If necessary for notifying the fact that an investigation agency, etc. is provided with communication user information under paragraph (1), the investigation agency, etc. may request for the confirmation of the relevant matters specified in the following subparagraphs; in such cases, the telecommunications business operator in receipt of such request shall comply therewith, except in extenuating circumstances:
Where such request is made to a telecommunications business operator who has provided communication user information under Article 83 (3): Whether there is any change in the communication user information of the person who is the subject of the information;
Where such request is made to any other telecommunications business operator: whether the person who is the subject of the communication user information is a user of the relevant telecommunications business.
If necessary for notifying the fact that an investigation agency, etc. is provided with communication user information under paragraph (1), the investigation agency, etc. may request the Minister of the Interior and Safety to provide electronic data of resident registration referred to in Article 30 (1) of the Resident Registration Act . In such cases, the Minister in receipt of such request shall comply with the request, except in extenuating circumstances.
Notwithstanding Article 30 (6) of the Resident Registration Act , fees for the provision of electronic data of resident registration under paragraph (6) shall be exempted.
Matters necessary for procedures for notifying the fact that communication user information is provided under paragraph (1) and procedures, etc. for deferring notice under paragraphs (2) and (3) shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree.
[This Article Added on Dec. 29, 2023]

