text_en:
Article 83-4 (Management and supervision with respect to the agency)
The investigation agency, etc. may manage and supervise the following with respect to the Agency, as prescribed by Presidential Decree, and request the Agency to submit materials necessary therefor or may inspect the performance of agency services:
Matters regarding whether notice on the fact that communication user information is given and whether methods and procedures for notifying the fact are appropriate;
Matters regarding institutional and technical security measures to prevent the leakage of communications user information provided through information and communications networks, etc.;
Matters regarding whether the Agency is capable of performing the tasks and whether it maintains relevant technology;
Matters regarding the management, etc. under Article 83-3 (4) of the notice management ledger and materials related to the notification that notice of the fact is deferred.
The investigation agency, etc. may request the Agency to make correction as prescribed by Presidential Decree if the Agency falls under any of the following cases:
Where it fails to keep the notice management ledger or materials related to the notification that the notice of the fact is deferred, in violation of Article 83-3 (4);
Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as where it fails to take institutional and technical security measures to prevent the leakage of communications user information provided through information and communications networks, etc.;
[This Article Added on Dec. 29, 2023]

