The Minister of Science and ICT or the Korea Media and Communications Commission may issue a corrective order to any of the following telecommunications business operators (including a person subject to investigation under the subparagraphs of Article 51 (2) in the case of a violation of Article 51 or an order issued thereunder; hereafter the same shall apply in this Article) or facility management authorities, based upon affairs falling under his or her or its jurisdiction. In such cases, where the Korea Media and Communications Commission issues a corrective order for violating Article 22-5 , it shall notify the Korea Communications Standards Commission established under Article 18 of the Act on the Establishment and Operation of Korea Media and Communications Commission of such fact: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Aug. 13, 2013; Oct. 15, 2014; Jan. 20, 2015; Dec. 1, 2015; Jan. 27, 2016; Jul. 26, 2017; Dec. 24, 2018; Jun. 9, 2020; Sep. 14, 2021; Jan. 3, 2023; Dec. 29, 2023; Jan. 21, 2025; Mar. 18, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
Where he or she violates Article 3 , 4, 4-2, 6, 9 through 11, 14 through 22, 22-3 through 22-5, 22-7 through 22-9, 22-11, 23, 24, 26 through 28, 30 through 32, 32-3, 32-4, 32-6, 32-7, 32-8, 32-10, 33 through 35, 35-2, 36 through 44, 47 through 49, 51, 56 through 60, 60-2, 60-3, 61, 62, 64 through 66, 69, 73 through 75, 79 or 82 through 84, 84-2, 85 through 87, and 88, or the orders issued under these provisions;
Where procedures for his or her business operations are deemed to inflict significant harm on the users' interests;
Where he or she fails to promptly take measures necessary for removing an obstruction, such as repair, when an accident, etc. impedes the provision of telecommunications services.
The Minister of Science and ICT may order a telecommunications business operator to perform any of the following affairs, when necessary for the development of telecommunications: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Aug. 13, 2013; Jul. 26, 2017>
Integrated operation and management of telecommunications equipment;
Expansion of communications facilities for the improvement of social welfare;
Establishment and management of communications networks for important communications prescribed by Presidential Decree which are necessary for efficient performance of the State's functions;
Other matters prescribed by Presidential Decree.
The Minister of Science and ICT may order any of the following persons to suspend the provision of telecommunications services or to take measures such as removing telecommunications equipment: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Oct. 15, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017; Dec. 24, 2018>
A person who operates the facilities-based telecommunications business without filing for registration under Article 6 (1);
